#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# array_rules

#% text
# `array_rules(a)` gives the list of rules `[i, j, ...] -> x` for the entries `x` of the array `a` that are not zero, followed by the rule `[_, _, ...] -> 0` for all other positions.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `array_rules(a, v)` takes `v` instead of 0 as the value of the other positions.

#% item
# `sparse_array(array_rules(a))` rebuilds the array.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
array_rules([[0, 1], [2, 0]])
#% output
#= [[1, 2] -> 1, [2, 1] -> 2, [_, _] -> 0]

#% cell
array_rules([1, 0, 0, 5])
#% output
#= [[1] -> 1, [4] -> 5, [_] -> 0]

#% cell
array_rules([[1, 1], [0, 1]], 1)
#% output
#= [[2, 1] -> 0, [_, _] -> 1]

#% cell
sparse_array(array_rules([[0, 1], [2, 0]])) == [[0, 1], [2, 0]]
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `sparse_array`, `position`, `dimensions`
